7	+---
8	+title: 'Add threshold validation to frai eval'
9	+type: 'feature'
10	+created: '2026-09-21'
11	+status: 'in-progress'
12	+review_loop_iteration: 0
13	+followup_review_recommended: false
14	+baseline_revision: '0ecac310b883c9afc2158332c59c0374802ace07'
15	+context: []
16	+warnings: []
17	+deferred: []
18	+---
19	+
20	+<intent-contract>
21	+
22	+## Intent
23	+
24	+**Problem:** Today `frai eval` always exits with code 0, so CI/CD pipelines cannot gate on metric quality. This blocks use cases where evaluation must fail the build when metrics fall below acceptable minimums.
25	+
26	+**Approach:** Add a `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable) to `frai eval` that validates metrics after evaluation. Embed the same logic in frai-core's `generateReport()` so SDK users can programmatically gate on metrics. Exit 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 for usage errors. Reports record outcome in both JSON and Markdown formats.
27	+
28	+## Boundaries & Constraints
29	+
30	+**Always:**
31	+- A threshold passes when the metric's score is ≥ the minimum value.
32	+- A metric with no score (e.g., exact_match without references) fails its threshold instead of crashing or silently passing.
33	+- Report is written regardless of threshold pass/fail status.
34	+- Without `--threshold`, behavior and exit codes are identical to today (backward compatible).
35	+- Custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations()` in frai-core must support thresholds.
36	+- Threshold option format: `<metric>=<number>` where number is in range [0, 1].
37	+
38	+**Never:**
39	+- Do not apply thresholds before evaluation completes (must evaluate all metrics first).
40	+- Do not break existing APIs; only add optional parameters.
41	+- Do not allow threshold values outside [0, 1] range.
42	+- Do not add new required fields to metric objects.
43	+
44	+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
45	+
46	+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
47	+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
48	+| Valid threshold, passes | `--threshold exact_match=0.8` with score 0.9 | Exit 0, report shows threshold passed | No error |
49	+| Valid threshold, fails | `--threshold exact_match=0.9` with score 0.8 | Exit 1, report shows threshold failed | No error; report still written |
50	+| Multiple thresholds, all pass | `--threshold exact_match=0.8 --threshold toxicity=0.9` | Exit 0, all thresholds recorded as passed | No error |
51	+| Multiple thresholds, one fails | `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.8` with EM=0.7, tox=0.95 | Exit 1, report shows EM failed | No error; report still written |
52	+| Metric has no score | `--threshold exact_match=0.8` but metric not computed | Threshold fails (no score = fail) | Exit 1; report records score as null/missing |
53	+| Unknown metric in threshold | `--threshold unknown_metric=0.8` | Exit 2, error message lists valid metric ids | No report written |
54	+| Malformed threshold format | `--threshold exact_match-0.8` or `--threshold exact_match` | Exit 2, error message explains format | No report written |
55	+| Threshold value out of range | `--threshold exact_match=1.5` or `--threshold exact_match=-0.1` | Exit 2, error message says 0–1 only | No report written |
56	+| No thresholds provided | Normal eval run | Exit 0 or 1 based on evaluation, no threshold data in report | Backward compatible |
57	+
58	+</intent-contract>
59	+
60	+## Code Map
61	+
62	+- `{project-root}/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` -- CLI entry point; add `--threshold` option to eval command (lines ~709–717) and pass parsed thresholds to runEvalCommand (lines ~476–497)
63	+- `{project-root}/packages/frai-cli/src/eval.ts` (or .js) -- runEvalCommand implementation; parse threshold option, call frai-core's generateReport with thresholds, handle exit codes 0/1/2
64	+- `{project-root}/packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js` -- generateReport() function; accept optional thresholds object, validate and apply thresholds, populate report.passed and report.thresholds
65	+- `{project-root}/packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js` -- toJson() and toMarkdown(); include passed boolean and thresholds list in JSON; add "Thresholds" section to Markdown showing PASS/FAIL per threshold
66	+- `{project-root}/packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` -- metric structure reference; no changes needed but confirms metric.score field and that custom metrics use same structure
67	+
68	+## Tasks & Acceptance
69	+
70	+**Execution:**
71	+
72	+- `{project-root}/packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js` -- Add optional `thresholds` parameter to `generateReport(report, options)` where options.thresholds = { metric_id: min_value }. Validate each threshold is a number in [0, 1]. For each threshold, check report.results[metric_id].score; if missing or null, mark as failed. Populate report.passed (boolean) and report.thresholds (array of { metric, min, score, passed }) before returning. -- Ensures SDK users can gate on thresholds programmatically; report structure change is minimal and optional.
73	+
74	+- `{project-root}/packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js` -- Modify toJson() to include report.passed and report.thresholds at top level. Modify toMarkdown() to append a "Thresholds" section (if report.thresholds exists) with a table or list showing metric, min, score, and PASS/FAIL status. -- Reports become actionable; users can see at a glance why a build failed.
75	+
76	+- `{project-root}/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (or wherever eval command is defined) -- Add `.option('--threshold <metric>=<min>', 'Minimum score threshold for metric', (val, acc) => [...acc, val], [])` to the eval command definition. Store as array of strings like ['exact_match=0.9', 'toxicity=0.8']. -- CLI exposes the feature to users.
77	+
78	+- `{project-root}/packages/frai-cli/src/eval.ts` (or runEvalCommand location) -- Parse threshold option strings: split on '=', validate format and value range, build thresholds object. Call generateReport(report, { thresholds: parsedThresholds }). Check report.passed; exit 0 if true, 1 if false. On parsing error, log error message listing valid metric ids, exit 2, do not write report. -- CLI enforces correct usage and exit codes.
79	+
80	+**Acceptance Criteria:**
81	+
82	+- **Given** a frai eval invocation with `--threshold exact_match=0.8`, **when** evaluation completes with exact_match score 0.9, **then** exit 0 and report includes `"passed": true` and `"thresholds": [{ metric: "exact_match", min: 0.8, score: 0.9, passed: true }]`
83	+
84	+- **Given** a frai eval invocation with `--threshold exact_match=0.9`, **when** evaluation completes with exact_match score 0.8, **then** exit 1 and report includes `"passed": false` and threshold marked failed
85	+
86	+- **Given** a frai eval invocation with `--threshold unknown_metric=0.5`, **when** the command runs, **then** exit 2, error message lists valid metric ids (exact_match, toxicity, length_variance), and no report is written
87	+
88	+- **Given** a frai eval invocation with `--threshold exact_match=malformed`, **when** the command runs, **then** exit 2, error message explains format is `<metric>=<number>`, and no report is written
89	+
90	+- **Given** a frai eval invocation with `--threshold exact_match=1.5`, **when** the command runs, **then** exit 2, error message says threshold must be 0–1, and no report is written
91	+
92	+- **Given** a frai eval invocation with multiple thresholds `--threshold exact_match=0.8 --threshold toxicity=0.9`, **when** one fails and one passes, **then** exit 1 and report.passed is false
93	+
94	+- **Given** evaluation where exact_match metric has no score (references not provided), **when** `--threshold exact_match=0.5` is set, **then** threshold fails (score recorded as null) and report shows it failed
95	+
96	+- **Given** a normal frai eval with no `--threshold` options, **when** evaluation completes, **then** exit 0 or 1 based on evaluation status (unchanged), report has no passed/thresholds fields (backward compatible)
97	+
98	+- **Given** SDK code calling frai-core's `runEvaluations()` followed by `generateReport(report, { thresholds: { exact_match: 0.8 } })`, **when** generateReport returns, **then** report.passed and report.thresholds are populated correctly, even for custom metrics
99	+
100	+## Design Notes
101	+
102	+### Threshold Validation and Error Handling
103	+
104	+The feature distinguishes three exit cases:
105	+1. **Exit 0**: All thresholds passed (or no thresholds provided and evaluation succeeded).
106	+2. **Exit 1**: One or more thresholds failed (evaluation succeeded but quality gates did not).
107	+3. **Exit 2**: Malformed or invalid threshold (usage error; no report written).
108	+
109	+Exit 2 is used for:
110	+- Unknown metric id → error lists all valid ids (exact_match, toxicity, length_variance) + any custom metrics in report
111	+- Malformed format (not `<metric>=<number>`) → error explains format
112	+- Value out of range ([0, 1]) → error specifies valid range
113	+
114	+### No-Score Behavior
115	+
116	+When a metric has no score (e.g., exact_match without references):
117	+- The metric object's score field is null, undefined, or absent.
118	+- A threshold on that metric fails (does not pass) and is recorded with score: null.
119	+- This avoids silent passes and keeps CI gating predictable.
120	+
121	+### Report Structure
122	+
123	+**JSON:**
124	+```json
125	+{
126	+  "generatedAt": "2026-09-21T10:00:00Z",
127	+  "passed": true,
128	+  "thresholds": [
129	+    { "metric": "exact_match", "min": 0.8, "score": 0.9, "passed": true },
130	+    { "metric": "toxicity", "min": 0.85, "score": 0.92, "passed": true }
131	+  ],
132	+  "results": [...]
133	+}
134	+```
135	+
136	+**Markdown:**
137	+```
138	+## Thresholds
139	+
140	+| Metric | Min | Score | Status |
141	+|--------|-----|-------|--------|
142	+| exact_match | 0.8 | 0.9 | PASS |
143	+| toxicity | 0.85 | 0.92 | PASS |
144	+```
145	+
146	+### Backward Compatibility
147	+
148	+Without `--threshold` options, no passed/thresholds fields are added to the report. Existing scripts and parsers are unaffected. The feature is purely additive.
149	+
150	+## Verification
151	+
152	+**Commands:**
153	+
154	+- `cd {project-root} && npm test` (or `pnpm test`) -- Verify frai-core tests pass, including new unit tests for threshold validation logic in generateReport()
155	+
156	+- `cd {project-root}/packages/frai-cli && npm run build` -- Verify CLI compiles without errors
157	+
158	+- `cd {project-root} && node frai.mjs eval --outputs examples/outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --report /tmp/report.json` -- Verify exit code 1 if exact_match < 0.9, inspect report for passed/thresholds fields
159	+
160	+- `cd {project-root} && node frai.mjs eval --outputs examples/outputs.json --threshold invalid_metric=0.5` -- Verify exit 2 and error message lists valid metrics
161	+
162	+- `cd {project-root} && node frai.mjs eval --outputs examples/outputs.json --threshold exact_match=bad` -- Verify exit 2 and error message explains format
163	+
164	+- `cd {project-root} && node frai.mjs eval --outputs examples/outputs.json --format markdown --threshold exact_match=0.8 --report /tmp/report.md` -- Verify Markdown report includes Thresholds section with PASS/FAIL status
