20	+<intent-contract>
21	+
22	+## Intent
23	+
24	+**Problem:** Today `frai eval` always exits with code 0, so CI/CD pipelines cannot gate on metric quality. This blocks use cases where evaluation must fail the build when metrics fall below acceptable minimums.
25	+
26	+**Approach:** Add a `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable) to `frai eval` that validates metrics after evaluation. Embed the same logic in frai-core's `generateReport()` so SDK users can programmatically gate on metrics. Exit 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 for usage errors. Reports record outcome in both JSON and Markdown formats.
27	+
28	+## Boundaries & Constraints
29	+
30	+**Always:**
31	+- A threshold passes when the metric's score is ≥ the minimum value.
32	+- A metric with no score (e.g., exact_match without references) fails its threshold instead of crashing or silently passing.
33	+- Report is written regardless of threshold pass/fail status.
34	+- Without `--threshold`, behavior and exit codes are identical to today (backward compatible).
35	+- Custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations()` in frai-core must support thresholds.
36	+- Threshold option format: `<metric>=<number>` where number is in range [0, 1].
37	+
38	+**Never:**
39	+- Do not apply thresholds before evaluation completes (must evaluate all metrics first).
40	+- Do not break existing APIs; only add optional parameters.
41	+- Do not allow threshold values outside [0, 1] range.
42	+- Do not add new required fields to metric objects.
43	+
44	+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
45	+
46	+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
47	+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
48	+| Valid threshold, passes | `--threshold exact_match=0.8` with score 0.9 | Exit 0, report shows threshold passed | No error |
49	+| Valid threshold, fails | `--threshold exact_match=0.9` with score 0.8 | Exit 1, report shows threshold failed | No error; report still written |
50	+| Multiple thresholds, all pass | `--threshold exact_match=0.8 --threshold toxicity=0.9` | Exit 0, all thresholds recorded as passed | No error |
51	+| Multiple thresholds, one fails | `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.8` with EM=0.7, tox=0.95 | Exit 1, report shows EM failed | No error; report still written |
52	+| Metric has no score | `--threshold exact_match=0.8` but metric not computed | Threshold fails (no score = fail) | Exit 1; report records score as null/missing |
53	+| Unknown metric in threshold | `--threshold unknown_metric=0.8` | Exit 2, error message lists valid metric ids | No report written |
54	+| Malformed threshold format | `--threshold exact_match-0.8` or `--threshold exact_match` | Exit 2, error message explains format | No report written |
55	+| Threshold value out of range | `--threshold exact_match=1.5` or `--threshold exact_match=-0.1` | Exit 2, error message says 0–1 only | No report written |
56	+| No thresholds provided | Normal eval run | Exit 0 or 1 based on evaluation, no threshold data in report | Backward compatible |
57	+
58	+</intent-contract>
